  "kind": "bit-matching-detail",
  "title": "PHI computes x87 sq = x*x (#NUM! on overflow), EXP(-sq/2) * 0x3fd9884533d43651, and flushes subnormals to +0",
  "statement": "In Excel 16.0.20131 through 16.0.20527, PHI(x) forms sq = RN53(RN64(x * x)) (rejecting overflow with #NUM!), evaluates e = EXP(-sq / 2), multiplies by the reciprocal constant RN(1/sqrt(2*pi)) = 0x3fd9884533d43651 in x87 (rather than dividing by sqrt(2*pi)), and flushes subnormal results to +0.0 (so PHI(37.8511319) = 0). Under compat-1, @PHI returns #NAME?.",
  "status": "measured",
  "basis": "Measured across Excel 16.0.20131, 20430, and 20527.20088, matching 14,406/14,406 full-bank and 120/120 pinned PHI rows.",
